          "attrs": {
            "style": "x",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "\n",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "DAN.7.9+DAN.7.10"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Dan 7.9–10",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "\n",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Then I saw a great white throne and the one who sits on it. Earth and heaven fled from his presence and were seen no more. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "REV.20.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "REV.20.11"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "12",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "REV 20:12"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "12",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And I saw the dead, great and small alike, standing before the throne. Books were opened, and then another book was opened, the book of the living. The dead were judged according to what they had done, as recorded in the books. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "REV.20.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "REV.20.12"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "13",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "REV 20:13"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "13",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Then the sea gave up its dead. Death and the world of the dead also gave up the dead they held. And all were judged according to what they had done. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "REV.20.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "REV.20.13"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "14",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "REV 20:14"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "14",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Then death and the world of the dead were thrown into the lake of fire. (This lake of fire is the second death.) ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "REV.20.14",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "REV.20.14"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "15",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "REV 20:15"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "15",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Whoever did not have their names written in the book of the living were thrown into the lake of fire.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "REV.20.15",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "REV.20.15"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    }
